@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@
+---
+title: Lizard
+icon: '/logo/integrations/lizard.svg'
+description: Run Roomote tasks in Lizard Firecracker microVM sandboxes.
+---
+
+Lizard is a hosted sandbox provider for running Roomote tasks away from the
+Roomote server. Each sandbox is a Firecracker microVM with its own kernel,
+billed per second while it runs.
+
+## When to use Lizard
+
+Use Lizard when:
+
+- task work should run on provider-managed microVMs with strong isolation
+- you want API-key-only setup without building a provider-side worker image
+  during Roomote setup
+- sandboxes should boot in well under a second from a catalog template
+- environments need per-port preview URLs
+- you want both environment snapshots and same-sandbox standby resume
+
+Lizard is the only provider in Roomote that supports snapshots **and** standby
+resume **and** per-port previews. It does not run Docker projects: the catalog
+templates have no Docker daemon.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Create an API key from the [Lizard dashboard](https://lizard.build/dashboard),
+then add Lizard from **Settings > Sandboxes**. Every sandbox must be billed to a
+project, so the project ID or slug is required too. You can also provide both as
+deployment env vars:
+
+```sh
+DEFAULT_COMPUTE_PROVIDER=lizard
+LIZARD_API_KEY=...
+LIZARD_PROJECT=...
+```
+
+Optional settings:
+
+```sh
+# Catalog template to boot. Defaults to interpreter, which ships Node 22 and
+# Python. base, claude, and opencode are also usable.
+LIZARD_TEMPLATE=interpreter
+# nano, mini, small, medium, large, or big. Defaults to the smallest size that
+# satisfies the task's memory requirement.
+LIZARD_SIZE=small
+# Active sandbox timeout in milliseconds. Defaults to 2 hours. The Lizard
+# trial caps sandbox lifetime at 1 hour.
+LIZARD_TIMEOUT_MS=...
+# Standby retention policy. Defaults to 10 paused sandboxes for 168 hours.
+# Set the count to 0 to disable retained task sandboxes.
+LIZARD_STANDBY_MAX_COUNT=10
+LIZARD_STANDBY_MAX_AGE_HOURS=168
+```
+
+These optional values are also available under **Settings > Sandboxes >
+Lizard > Advanced settings**. Process environment variables take precedence and
+appear as locked values in Settings.
+
+Roomote does not provision a worker artifact in your Lizard account during
+setup. Saving a valid API key and project is enough to configure the provider.
+
+Roomote installs its worker into each sandbox when it starts. The worker archive
+is uploaded through the Lizard filesystem API and installed by the shipped
+`install-worker.sh`, so no custom template upload is needed.
+
+## Sizes and cost
+
+Lizard bills per second while a sandbox runs. The flat hourly prices are:
+
+| Size   | vCPU | Memory | Disk | Price per hour |
+| ------ | ---- | ------ | ---- | -------------- |
+| Nano   | 0.5  | 1 GB   | 5 GB | $0.00405       |
+| Mini   | 1    | 2 GB   | 10 GB | $0.0081       |
+| Small  | 2    | 4 GB   | 20 GB | $0.0162       |
+| Medium | 4    | 8 GB   | 40 GB | $0.0324       |
+| Large  | 8    | 16 GB  | 80 GB | $0.0648       |
+| Big    | 16   | 32 GB  | 120 GB | $0.1296      |
+
+Paused sandboxes and snapshots cost $0.14 per GB-month of used disk. The trial
+runs 1 Small, 2 Mini, and 2 Nano sandboxes at a time in US regions only, and
+deletes each sandbox one hour after it starts.
+
+## Cleanup and resume behavior
+
+Roomote pauses a Lizard sandbox when retaining it for task resume. Pausing stops
+compute billing, keeps the sandbox's files, and ends running processes. A
+follow-up resume boots the sandbox fresh from its files and relaunches the
+worker.
+
+`LIZARD_STANDBY_MAX_COUNT` and `LIZARD_STANDBY_MAX_AGE_HOURS` bound how many
+paused sandboxes Roomote retains and for how long. This standby behavior
+preserves one task's machine; it is not a Roomote environment snapshot.
+
+## Environment snapshots
+
+Roomote environment snapshots map to Lizard snapshots: snapshotting an
+environment saves a `roomote-snap-*` snapshot of the whole disk, and tasks that
+start from it restore a fresh sandbox in well under a second instead of
+re-running environment setup. Snapshots restore only inside the snapshot's own
+project and region.
+
+## Verify setup
+
+1. Save the Lizard API key and project.
+2. Select Lizard as the default sandbox provider.
+3. Start a small task and confirm logs reach the task view.
+4. If the environment exposes a port, open its preview from the task view.
+5. Send a follow-up while the task sandbox is retained and confirm it resumes.
+
+## Common issues
+
+- **Authentication fails.** Confirm `LIZARD_API_KEY` is active and belongs to
+  the expected Lizard account.
+- **Sandbox creation fails with a project error.** Set `LIZARD_PROJECT` to the
+  project ID or slug the sandboxes should bill to.
+- **The worker install fails.** The chosen catalog template must ship Node. Use
+  `interpreter` (the default), `claude`, or `opencode`.
+- **A task stops after one hour.** Trial accounts cap sandbox lifetime at one
+  hour. Start a paid plan or reduce `LIZARD_TIMEOUT_MS`.
+- **A follow-up starts a new sandbox.** Check the standby count and age limits.
+  Roomote may no longer retain the previous sandbox as the task's resume target.
+- **A preview does not open.** Confirm the environment declares the port and the
+  application listens on `0.0.0.0`, not only `localhost`.
+- **Docker projects fail.** Lizard catalog templates have no Docker daemon.
+  Choose a provider with Docker support for those environments.
